# Copy this file to .env.local for local development (.env.local is
# git-ignored). Never commit real values.
#
# Both variables below are PUBLIC values by design: the Supabase "anon" key
# is meant to ship in client bundles and is only ever as powerful as your
# Row Level Security policies allow (see docs/SECURITY.md). Do NOT put the
# service-role key here or anywhere under src/ - it belongs exclusively in
# Supabase Edge Function secrets (see README.md "Umgebungsvariablen & Secrets").
#
# Enter both values BARE: no surrounding quotes, no line breaks, and no Markdown
# link syntax. Copying "[https://ref.supabase.co](https://ref.supabase.co)" out
# of a rendered document is a real and hard-to-spot failure mode - a substring
# search still finds the URL in the built bundle, but every request fails at the
# network layer. src/lib/supabaseConfig.ts rejects such values at startup.

# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Project Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public
# (current format: sb_publishable_..., legacy format: an anon JWT)
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional later dual-read (Phase 1 lexicon stays on catalog.ts + published.json).
# Values: legacy (default) | postgres
# VITE_RESEARCH_DB_MODE=legacy
